<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51450" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vulturnālis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Volt-</span></b> ), e,
		adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the god Vulturnus</i>
			(perh. the same as Vertumnus). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: flamen, Enn. ap. <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, § 45</span></i>
			Müll. (Ann. v. 125 Vahl.).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vulturnālia</span></b> , ĭum,
				n., <i>the festival of Vulturnus</i>,
			acc. to <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 379</span></i> Müll.</div>
